+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+For Porter II EV conventional cruise, the value times 0.01s remains bounded to 40–60ms and two or three fresh samples. Skip a new sample when consecutive positive automatic requests at the actual host dispatch clock would be less than 15ms apart. Preserve ordinary approximately 19–20ms spacing, without replaying skipped samples later or extending press deadlines or frame budgets. Release and driver, brake or cancel interruptions do not wait for this spacing guard. This does not guarantee wire timing or ECU acceptance.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Existing request spacing and response waits remain. This setting does not bypass MAIN, pedal or brake conditions.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+This is a Porter-specific host bound; it adds no new limit to other Hyundai/Kia paths.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
